+++ b/docs/mining-outage-acceptance.md
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+# Collector loss during actual mining
+
+2026-10-03. The bounded local acceptance test passes with actual efsn mining,
+automatic ticket purchases, nginx WSS, the collector, PostgreSQL and HTTPS API.
+Only dashboard test code changes in this slice. Dashboard application code, dependencies, schema,
+compiled frontend and nginx configuration remain unchanged.
+The efsn node has a separate two-line reporting correction, P17: queued head
+notifications now read the current canonical tip. The baseline reported height
+73 followed by obsolete queued height 62; collector snapshots briefly showed 62.
+This changes telemetry only, including after recovery; chain state, mining,
+tickets and consensus are unchanged. Genuine reorganizations still report their
+actual tip, even if height decreases. The final test rejects the old report and
+checks the persisted contiguous forty-block chart after history recovery.
+
+`test/efsn-mining-outage.test.cjs` runs on Linux. It starts the collector separately
+from the proxy, writer and API, then terminates only the collector process. The
+same efsn process stays alive with mining and automatic purchases enabled. After
+twelve further blocks it starts a fresh collector on the original port with the
+same synthetic credential. Neither the node nor writer is restarted or manually
+reconnected. The independent processes use one Linux clock.
+
+The corrected run records:
+
+- Height 61 before loss, height 73 before restoration, height 74 after recovery.
+  The account nonce advances 61 → 73 → 74 and retains two tickets. All thirteen
+  intervening canonical blocks contain one successful ticket purchase by the
+  public test account, with consecutive nonces and native purchase receipts.
+- The collector port refuses connections throughout the measured outage. The
+  stored snapshot stops changing; all four API views return HTTP 503 after the
+  ten-second snapshot budget. Mining and automatic purchases stay enabled.
+- The outage lasts 141.949 seconds. A fresh authenticated report covering the
+  next mined block reaches HTTPS in 12.267 seconds after collector restoration.
+  The normal history request subsequently supplies fifty missing blocks. Together
+  with individual head reports, these cover all twelve outage blocks. Head/history hashes and transaction hashes
+  agree with direct RPC at those specific heights.
+- Twenty-seven snapshots are saved, at most 6,166 bytes. The test writer retries
+  every 250 ms and records 544 expected connection-loss/failure messages. It
+  reports no other error category and no new errors after recovery. This short
+  test interval is not a public retry/log-volume recommendation.
+- The corrected reconnect head sequence is 73, 73, 74, 74. Every captured
+  nonempty collector snapshot stays at or above 73. The recovered persisted
+  chart contains heights 35–74 with exactly one transaction per block.
+
+The first attempt passed block production, stale API and head recovery checks,
+then asserted the presence of history before the next normal latency report.
+The final test waits, bounded to 25 seconds, for that existing history cycle.
+The second run passes liveness but exposes the queued-head reporting defect
+during the subsequent evidence audit. The corrected third run adds the head
+ordering and chart recovery assertions. All attempts and shutdowns are retained;
+no freshness or consensus rule is relaxed.
+
+The stationary WSS/PostgreSQL/Edge integration also passes its original four
+browser checkpoints with the updated Go fixture; 173 contract and 13 socket
+tests pass. That browser run is separate from the live outage drill. Public
+certificate acceptance and renewal are still untested; local certificates are
+verified against a temporary test CA, and the separate Edge fixture uses its
+existing temporary leaf-SPKI exception.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+Build the existing efsn `tests/restart` package with Go 1.21.3 and CGO enabled.
+The opt-in `TestDashboardTelemetryNode` supports `Mining: true` in its fixture
+settings, public key 1 only, a numeric loopback collector, and no backup input.
+It seeds sixty synthetic blocks before starting the ordinary miner and ticket
+buyer; it does not import manufactured blocks during the outage. The test uses
+the existing development-chain rules and leaves the block period unchanged.
+
+Run the new test with Node 22.11.0 on Linux:
+
+```text
+node --test --test-reporter=tap test/efsn-mining-outage.test.cjs
+```
+
+Supply absolute paths through `EFSN_TELEMETRY_BINARY`,
+`EFSN_TELEMETRY_EVIDENCE`, `EFSN_TLS_CA`, `EFSN_TLS_CERT`, `EFSN_TLS_KEY`,
+`EFSN_TLS_OUTPUT` and `TEST_NGINX`; set `TEST_PG_PORT` and
+`TEST_PG_PASSWORD_FILE` for a fresh loopback PostgreSQL database. The API/writer
+fixture creates its schema there. It uses the same extracted nginx and Linux
+PostgreSQL runtimes as the previous actual-WSS acceptance.
+
+The efsn repository's
+`docs/evidence/restart-dashboard-mining-outage-2026-10-03/run.py` creates the
+temporary certificates/database, captures runtime/source/build hashes and runs
+this test. `run-stationary.py` and `run-contracts.py` retain the regression
+results. `run-fixed.py` and `run-stationary-fixed.py` use the corrected efsn binary.
+`verify.py` ties the results to the committed patch and P17 source, while checking
+all other production sources remain unchanged. All five databases are stopped, temporary private files
+are removed and no matching test processes remain.
+
+This covers collector process loss and return with valid ordinary telemetry.
+It does not establish host supervision, certificate renewal, a supported public
+runtime matrix, production retry/log policy, or long-duration availability.
diff --git a/test/efsn-mining-outage.test.cjs b/test/efsn-mining-outage.test.cjs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f0c30cd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/efsn-mining-outage.test.cjs
@@ -0,0 +1,233 @@
+const assert = require('node:assert/strict');
+const { test } = require('node:test');
+const { once } = require('node:events');
+const { spawn } = require('node:child_process');
+const { readFileSync, writeFileSync, existsSync, mkdtempSync, unlinkSync, rmdirSync } = require('node:fs');
+const { join } = require('node:path');
+const { tmpdir } = require('node:os');
+const { createConnection } = require('node:net');
+const { Pool } = require('pg');
+const Retrieve = require('../db_methods/retrieve');
+const startCollector = require('./fixtures/collector-wire.cjs');
+const startTlsApi = require('./fixtures/efsn-tls-api.cjs');
+const { secretA } = require('./fixtures/collector.cjs');
+const request = require('./fixtures/http.cjs');
+
+async function waitFor(predicate, timeout = 25000) {
+    const deadline = Date.now() + timeout;
+    while (Date.now() < deadline) {
+        const result = await predicate();
+        if (result) {
+            return result;
+        }
+        await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 250));
+    }
+    throw new Error('Live mining observation deadline exceeded');
+}
+
+async function rpc(endpoint, method, params = []) {
+    const response = await fetch(endpoint, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify({ jsonrpc: '2.0', id: 1, method, params }), signal: AbortSignal.timeout(3000) });
+    const result = await response.json();
+    assert.equal(result.error, undefined, method);
+    return result.result;
+}
+
+function refusedPort(port) {
+    return new Promise(resolve => {
+        const socket = createConnection({ host: '127.0.0.1', port });
+        socket.once('connect', () => { socket.destroy(); resolve(false); });
+        socket.once('error', error => { socket.destroy(); resolve(error.code === 'ECONNREFUSED'); });
+        socket.setTimeout(500, () => { socket.destroy(); resolve(false); });
+    });
+}
+
+test('ordinary mining and purchases continue through collector process loss and WSS recovery', { timeout: 340000 }, async t => {
+    assert.equal(process.platform, 'linux');
+    for (const name of ['EFSN_TELEMETRY_BINARY', 'EFSN_TELEMETRY_EVIDENCE', 'TEST_PG_PORT', 'TEST_PG_PASSWORD_FILE', 'EFSN_TLS_CA', 'EFSN_TLS_CERT', 'EFSN_TLS_KEY', 'EFSN_TLS_OUTPUT', 'TEST_NGINX']) {
+        assert.ok(process.env[name], name);
+    }
+    const output = process.env.EFSN_TELEMETRY_EVIDENCE;
+    const ca = readFileSync(process.env.EFSN_TLS_CA);
+    const evidence = { phases: [], purchases: [], passed: false };
+    const save = (name, value) => writeFileSync(join(output, name + '.json'), JSON.stringify(value, null, 2) + '\n', 'utf8');
+    const cleanup = [];
+    let node;
+    let nodeExit;
+    let logs = '';
+    let server;
+    let tls;
+    let directory;
+    t.after(async () => {
+        try {
+            if (node && node.exitCode === null && node.signalCode === null) {
+                writeFileSync(join(directory, 'stop'), '', 'utf8');
+                await Promise.race([nodeExit, new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(() => { node.kill('SIGTERM'); resolve(); }, 8000).unref())]);
+            }
+            if (nodeExit) {
+                evidence.nodeExit = await nodeExit;
+            }
+            for (const close of cleanup.reverse()) {
+                await close();
+            }
+        } finally {
+            assert.equal(logs.includes(secretA), false);
+            writeFileSync(join(output, 'efsn.txt'), logs, 'utf8');
+            save('result-mining', { ...evidence, writer: tls && tls.state });
+            if (directory) {
+                for (const name of ['settings.json', 'ready.json', 'stop']) {
+                    if (existsSync(join(directory, name))) {
+                        unlinkSync(join(directory, name));
+                    }
+                }
+                rmdirSync(directory);
+            }
+        }
+    });
+    const settings = { COLLECTOR_MAX_MESSAGE_BYTES: '4194304', COLLECTOR_MAX_HEAD_BYTES: '65536', COLLECTOR_MAX_BUFFERED_BYTES: '1048576' };
+    server = await startCollector(t, settings, 'efsn-wire-server.cjs', { 'node-a': secretA });
+    const port = server.port;
+    const pool = new Pool({ host: '127.0.0.1', port: Number(process.env.TEST_PG_PORT), database: 'postgres', user: 'dashboard_test_admin', password: readFileSync(process.env.TEST_PG_PASSWORD_FILE, 'utf8'), connectionTimeoutMillis: 2000, statement_timeout: 2000, query_timeout: 2000 });
+    cleanup.push(() => pool.end());
+    await pool.query(readFileSync(join(__dirname, '../db/schema/001-dashboard.sql'), 'utf8'));
+    const retrieve = new Retrieve(pool);
+    tls = await startTlsApi(port, cleanup);
+    tls.startCollection();
+    directory = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'efsn-mining-dashboard-'));
+    writeFileSync(join(directory, 'settings.json'), JSON.stringify({ Collector: `wss://127.0.0.1:${tls.address.tlsPort}`, Secret: secretA, TransactionsPerBlock: 1, Mining: true }), { encoding: 'utf8', mode: 0o600 });
+    node = spawn(process.env.EFSN_TELEMETRY_BINARY, ['-test.run=^TestDashboardTelemetryNode$', '-test.v', '-test.timeout=370s'], { env: { ...process.env, GOMAXPROCS: '2', SSL_CERT_FILE: process.env.EFSN_TLS_CA, FUSION_DASHBOARD_FIXTURE: directory, FUSION_RESTART_CHAINDATA: '' }, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });
+    nodeExit = once(node, 'exit');
+    node.stdout.on('data', data => { logs += data; });
+    node.stderr.on('data', data => { logs += data; });
+    const ready = await waitFor(() => {
+        assert.equal(node.exitCode, null, logs);
+        return existsSync(join(directory, 'ready.json')) && JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(directory, 'ready.json'), 'utf8'));
+    });
+    evidence.ready = ready;
+    const read = (method, params) => rpc(ready.rpc, method, params);
+    async function observe(label) {
+        const head = await read('eth_getBlockByNumber', ['latest', false]);
+        const number = Number(BigInt(head.number));
+        const observation = { label, time: Date.now(), head, number,
+            mining: await read('eth_mining'), autoBuy: await read('fsn_isAutoBuyTicket'), peers: await read('net_peerCount'),
+            nonce: await read('eth_getTransactionCount', [ready.owner, head.number]),
+            tickets: await read('fsn_totalNumberOfTicketsByAddress', [ready.owner, head.number]) };
+        assert.equal(observation.mining, true);
+        assert.equal(observation.autoBuy, true);
+        assert.equal(BigInt(observation.peers), 0n);
+        assert.ok(observation.tickets > 0);
+        evidence.phases.push(observation);
+        return observation;
+    }
+    async function freshSnapshot(minimum) {
+        return waitFor(async () => {
+            const response = await request(tls.address.tlsPort, '/stats-api/nodes', ca);
+            assert.equal(response.tls.authorized, true);
+            if (response.status !== 200 || response.body.length !== 1) {
+                return false;
+            }
+            const value = JSON.parse(response.body[0].stats);
+            if (!value.connected || !value.stats.mining || value.stats.block.number < minimum || !Object.values(response.body[0].reportValidForMs).every(age => age > 0)) {
+                return false;
+            }
+            const block = await read('eth_getBlockByNumber', ['0x' + value.stats.block.number.toString(16), false]);
+            assert.equal(value.stats.block.hash, block.hash);
+            assert.equal(value.stats.block.parentHash, block.parentHash);
+            assert.deepEqual(value.stats.block.transactions.map(tx => tx.hash), block.transactions);
+            return { response, block, snapshot: await retrieve.readSnapshot() };
+        });
+    }
+    await freshSnapshot(61);
+    const before = await observe('before-outage');
+    save('collector-before', await server.command('capture'));
+    assert.deepEqual(tls.state.errors, []);
+    evidence.initialCollectorPid = server.pid;
+    await server.terminate();
+    evidence.outageStarted = Date.now();
+    assert.equal(await refusedPort(port), true);
+    const outageStart = await observe('collector-stopped');
+    const expired = await waitFor(async () => {
+        const response = await request(tls.address.tlsPort, '/stats-api/nodes', ca);
+        return response.status === 503 && response;
+    }, 16000);
+    assert.deepEqual(expired.body, { error: 'snapshot_unavailable' });
+    evidence.expired = { response: expired, time: Date.now() };
+    const stoppedSnapshot = await retrieve.readSnapshot();
+    await waitFor(async () => {
+        assert.equal(node.exitCode, null, logs);
+        return Number(BigInt(await read('eth_blockNumber'))) >= outageStart.number + 12;
+    }, 240000);
+    const during = await observe('twelve-blocks-without-collector');
+    assert.equal(await refusedPort(port), true);
+    assert.ok(during.number - outageStart.number >= 12);
+    assert.ok(BigInt(during.nonce) - BigInt(outageStart.nonce) >= 12n);
+    const retained = await retrieve.readSnapshot();
+    assert.deepEqual(retained, stoppedSnapshot);
+    for (const path of ['nodes', 'blocks', 'charts', 'info']) {
+        const response = await request(tls.address.tlsPort, '/stats-api/' + path, ca);
+        assert.equal(response.status, 503);
+        assert.deepEqual(response.body, { error: 'snapshot_unavailable' });
+    }
+    save('snapshot-retained-during-outage', retained);
+    server = await startCollector(t, { ...settings, COLLECTOR_PORT: String(port) }, 'efsn-wire-server.cjs', { 'node-a': secretA });
+    evidence.restoredAt = Date.now();
+    evidence.restoredCollectorPid = server.pid;
+    assert.equal(server.port, port);
+    assert.notEqual(server.pid, evidence.initialCollectorPid);
+    evidence.recoveredSnapshot = await freshSnapshot(during.number + 1);
+    evidence.recoveredAt = Date.now();
+    const captured = await waitFor(async () => {
+        const value = await server.command('capture');
+        return value.records.some(record => record.direction === 'incoming' && record.message.emit && record.message.emit[0] === 'history' && record.message.emit[1].history.length === 50) && value;
+    });
+    const after = await observe('recovered-with-next-mined-block');
+    assert.ok(after.number > during.number);
+    assert.ok(BigInt(after.nonce) > BigInt(during.nonce));
+    save('collector-after', captured);
+    const incoming = captured.records.filter(record => record.direction === 'incoming').map(record => record.message.emit).filter(Boolean);
+    assert.equal(incoming.filter(message => message[0] === 'hello').length, 1);
+    const history = incoming.find(message => message[0] === 'history' && message[1].history.length === 50);
+    assert.ok(history);
+    const liveBlocks = incoming.filter(message => message[0] === 'block').map(message => message[1].block);
+    assert.ok(liveBlocks.length > 0);
+    assert.ok(liveBlocks.every(block => block.number >= during.number));
+    evidence.recoveredHistorySnapshot = await waitFor(async () => {
+        const value = await freshSnapshot(after.number);
+        const heights = value.snapshot.payload.charts.height;
+        const latest = heights[heights.length - 1];
+        return heights.length === 40 && latest >= after.number && heights.every((height, index) => height === latest - 39 + index) && value;
+    });
+    for (const report of history[1].history) {
+        const block = await read('eth_getBlockByNumber', ['0x' + report.number.toString(16), false]);
+        assert.equal(report.hash, block.hash);
+        assert.equal(report.parentHash, block.parentHash);
+        assert.deepEqual(report.transactions.map(tx => tx.hash), block.transactions);
+    }
+    for (let number = before.number + 1; number <= after.number; number++) {
+        const block = await read('eth_getBlockByNumber', ['0x' + number.toString(16), true]);
+        const parent = await read('eth_getBlockByNumber', ['0x' + (number - 1).toString(16), false]);
+        assert.equal(block.parentHash, parent.hash);
+        assert.equal(block.miner.toLowerCase(), ready.owner.toLowerCase());
+        assert.equal(block.transactions.length, 1);
+        const tx = block.transactions[0];
+        assert.equal(tx.from.toLowerCase(), ready.owner.toLowerCase());
+        const receipt = await read('eth_getTransactionReceipt', [tx.hash]);
+        assert.equal(receipt.blockHash, block.hash);
+        assert.equal(receipt.status, '0x1');
+        const purchase = receipt.logs.map(log => {
+            try { return JSON.parse(Buffer.from(log.data.slice(2), 'hex').toString('utf8')); } catch (_) { return null; }
+        }).find(value => value && value.TicketID && value.TicketOwner);
+        assert.ok(purchase);
+        assert.equal(purchase.Error || '', '');
+        assert.equal(purchase.TicketOwner.toLowerCase(), ready.owner.toLowerCase());
+        evidence.purchases.push({ block, receipt, purchase });
+    }
+    const allowedErrors = new Set(['Collector connection closed unexpectedly', 'Collector connection failed']);
+    assert.ok(tls.state.errors.length > 0);
+    assert.ok(tls.state.errors.every(message => allowedErrors.has(message)), JSON.stringify([...new Set(tls.state.errors)]));
+    evidence.writerErrorsAfterRecovery = tls.state.errors.length;
+    await freshSnapshot(after.number);
+    assert.equal(tls.state.errors.length, evidence.writerErrorsAfterRecovery);
+    writeFileSync(join(directory, 'stop'), '', 'utf8');
+    assert.deepEqual(await nodeExit, [0, null]);
+    evidence.passed = true;
+});
diff --git a/test/fixtures/collector-wire.cjs b/test/fixtures/collector-wire.cjs
